{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-cursor-dao/open-argument-shapes-rw",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-CURSOR-1",
    "D-CURSOR-1",
    "CUR-PROV",
    "CUR-POS"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-cursor-1b/open-argument-shapes: the fixture was opened read-only, so Updatable read 0 for every shape. For each argument list of Database.OpenRecordset on a writable Database [\"F\" ;; SQL over F ;; \"QP\" (parameter query) ;; F, Long 0 ;; F, Long 1 ;; SQL, Long 1 ;; F, Integer 2 ;; F, \"2\" ;; F, Null ;; F, Empty ;; F, Long 3 ;; F, Long 5 ;; F, Long 16 ;; F, Long 32 ;; F, Missing, Long 4 ;; F, Long 2, Missing, Long 3 ;; F, Long 2, Long 0, Long 0 ;; F, Long 2, Long 0, Long 2, Long 0 ;; F, Long 8 ;; F, Long 2, Long 256 ;; \"\", Long 2 ;; NoSuch, Long 2 ;; Null, Long 2 ;; SQL WHERE 1 = 0, Long 4 ;; F, Long 2, Long 8]: call it, read Type, Updatable, Bookmarkable, EOF, RecordCount and Name; close. Nothing is written. Asks the default recordset type for a table name and for SQL, the refused type and option values, the accepted VARIANT types, omitted middle arguments and excess arguments, with Updatable on a writable open. The fixture copy is opened read-write.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
